WEBVTT

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:46.740
"I only received one New Year's card this year.  From a beauty salon..."

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:49.830
"I didn't receive a single one."

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:53.700
If anyone out there says any of that crap in the classroom after winter break,

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:56.000
starting next year, execute 'em!

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.570
That joke is as old as New Year's cards and beauty salons.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:04.250
It's too much effort to pretend to brag about that shit.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.040
I'm sick of it!

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.930
The practice of appearance for appearance's sake!

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:09.790
Enough of this farce!

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:12.970
Starting next year, execute every single person who sends a New Year's card!

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:14.780
Is that your final answer?

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:15.690
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.790
Execute away next year.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.230
All by yourself.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.690
Stop babbling like a kiddie.

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.020
Pen to the paper, pillar of society.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:28.030
Use a Calligraphy Pen for New Year's cards

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:31.920
Only received a card from a beauty salon?! Lame-o!

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:32.920
Idiots!

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.790
Why do people get so excited?!

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:35.950
Happy, my ass!

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:37.920
There's nothing to be happy about!

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:41.080
This show follows the Sazae-san format.
We're stuck in the same year forever!

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.620
It's a waste of time!

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:44.740
And why are we doing New Year's cards now?

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.000
We don't have a choice.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.520
The manga kept on rolling with seasonal material while we were on break.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.460
A year's worth of joy, all at once.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:51.990
Look.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.450
We got a bunch of cards from our clients.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:56.230
If we maintain a friendly relationship with our clients,

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.100
they might give us more work.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.100
One hour later...

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:03.630
There's no end in sight...

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:05.280
By the time I finish writing all these hope-you-have-a-great-years,

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.010
it'll already be next year.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:09.700
And why do you guys look like you're enjoying this?

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:10.670
Huh?

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:12.230
This isn't that bad.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:14.500
We get to catch up on what's happened.

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.410
You mean when they talk about starting a new life together

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:19.040
with a wedding picture attached?

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:22.750
<b>Happy New Year</b>

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:22.750
<b>We are blessed to celebrate our first New Year's together.</b>

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:22.750
<b>I hope that I will be able to serve as your editor for a very long time.</b>

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:22.750
<b>New Year's Day 2010</b>

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:22.750
<b>Atsushi and Chihiro Nakasaki</b>

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.210
You shouldn't assume that other people will be happy about your happiness, fool.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:24.490
Uh....

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:26.430
Wait, who is this?

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:27.250
And some people are like,

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:35.760
<b>Happy New Year</b>

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:35.760
<b>I appreciate everything</b>

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:35.760
<b>Kouhei Oonishi</b>

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:31.470
"We have a new member in the family!" with a picture of a baby.

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:33.620
Don't make it sound like this just magically happened.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.760
Just write that you had a baby after ****ing like rabbits.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.870
Nobody's going to say that on a New Year's card!

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:38.500
And who is this?

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:39.920
Who are these people?!

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:40.920
Also...

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.560
Don't bother if you're feeling lazy.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.020
You'll end up hurting someone's feelings.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:49.030
<b>Weekly Shounen Jump wants to thank you.</b>

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:49.030
<b>Yuu Saitou</b>

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:49.030
<b>Manuscripts are more important than your health!! -Saitou</b>

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:46.630
This wasn't sent to you, was it?

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:49.660
And those editors are seriously brutal!

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:55.480
But I like how New Year's cards are short and concise, unlike letters.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:56.540
Oh, look.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.300
There's one from Sakamoto-san.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.510
From Tatsuma?

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.960
Last year's Taiga drama was about me.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:04.220
What kind of message is that?!

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.310
He wants to fully exploit his brief surge in popularity!

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:08.900
You're getting another year of spot appearances in the openings and endings!

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.340
There's also one from Mutsu-san.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:13.320
Don't bother tearing this up.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.800
I also received cards from the Kaientai.

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:18.890
Why did they send cards to each of us?!

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:20.140
That's so obnoxious!

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:21.610
They're really dying for some screen time!

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:22.510
Wait...

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:24.090
There's a card from the Kiheitai!

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:24.730
Huh?!

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:25.800
From Takasugi?!

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.100
Happy New Year.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.330
I'll be destroying everything again this year.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.800
No way...

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:33.360
He sent a New Year's card?

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.850
Isn't this more like a declaration of war?

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:37.070
It might be a death threat.

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:39.450
<b>Matako Kijima, Bansai Kawakami, Henpeita Takechi</b>

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.450
The Kiheitai made an appearance in this year's Taiga drama.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.340
You too?!

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:43.930
Does everybody want more screen time?!

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:47.460
Oh, there's one from Katsura-san.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:48.370
What?

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:49.960
Zura gets plenty of screen time.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:54.280
I was on standby outside the entire time during the Santa episode.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:56.510
Like I give a damn!

00:04:56.510 --> 00:05:00.930
He never had a chance to jump in since
there were so many characters around.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.730
He sent a whole bunch.

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:05.020
<b>Has Lady Kyubei taken over the role of token hardhead?  {I shortened the timing on these lines so we wouldn't have the entire screen taken up with subs -laf}</b>

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:06.600
<b>I was on standby outside the entire time during the Santa episode.</b>

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:07.400
<b>You no longer need me with Lady Kyubei around?</b>

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.980
<b>I was on standby outside the entire time during the Santa episode.</b>

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:08.980
We already said that your characters don't overlap!

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:10.610
<b>I was a character in this show before Lady Kyubei was.</b>

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:10.610
You're just a psychotic moron!

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:13.280
Man, these people aren't taking this seriously.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:17.660
They make the silly Nakasaki couple look brilliant.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:21.330
Gin-san, someone else got married.

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:25.000
<b>Gintoki and Ayame Sakata</b>

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:23.220
We got married!

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:25.250
Guess I'm first, Otae.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:27.000
The hell is this?!

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:27.990
It's no use, Gin-san.

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:29.630
She sent a whole stack.

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:32.750
That bitch has really done it now!

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:33.910
Look at the shoddy picture!

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.880
That's somebody else's body below my face!

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.820
Someone sent a card to congratulate you.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.550
Congratulations!

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:42.220
Make sure you don't end up getting divorced.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:43.820
Ana Ketsuno!

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.570
What has she done?!

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.520
Looks like she sent them everywhere.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:52.940
<b>Hinowa</b>

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:49.830
Happy New Year.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:51.370
And congratulations on your marriage.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:51.820
This news will make Tsukuyo sad.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.580
May you be happy together!

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:57.780
<b>Seita</b>

00:05:53.570 --> 00:05:56.570
Ever since Tsukuyo heard that Gin-san got married, she's been feeling down.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:57.790
May you be happy together!

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:02.530
<b>Tsukyo</b>

00:05:58.490 --> 00:05:59.950
I appreciate your help last year.

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:01.350
Don't make your wife cry.

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:03.010
May you be happy together.

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:05.230
This is getting awkward...

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:08.930
It's obvious that Tsukuyo-san edited their cards.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:11.470
You also received one from the monkeys.

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:14.550
<b>Doesn't he look just like Shinpachi-kun?</b>

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:12.460
Congratulations!

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.550
I hope that our kids get to go to school together.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:17.420
How many steps did that stupid gorilla skip?!

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:18.910
Just like me?!

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:20.590
It is me!

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:21.710
Whoa.

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:24.190
He also sent his everywhere.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:29.850
<b>Strawberry milk</b>

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:26.150
Thank you for all the supportapoop!

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:27.300
I hope that you and the gorilla are happy together.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.180
Otsu-chan!

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:30.380
She's got this totally wrong!

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:31.010
Look.

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:32.500
There's one from the Yagyu household.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:33.860
I'm going to murder the gorilla.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.120
I'm going to murder the gorilla!

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.200
I'm going to murder Kondo!

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:36.940
Wait!

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:39.310
Kyubei-san's cards are the ones that need editing!

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:40.900
Her murderous rage is plain to see!

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:43.200
Gin-chan, here's another one from Zura.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:43.940
Why?!

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:46.850
Don't tell me that he's also lying about getting married...

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:50.450
I was on standby outside the entire time during the ceremony.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:52.300
The hell is he doing?!

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:53.990
Is he obsessed with being on standby?!

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:55.050
There was no ceremony!

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:57.270
And even if there was, it would have been too late!

00:06:57.270 --> 00:07:00.560
Hey, let's deal with these pains in the ass later.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:03.100
Start by replying to the normal people.

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:05.710
Do we know any normal people...?

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:06.720
No way!

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:07.810
This one's from Hijikata-san?

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:08.790
Whoa.

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:10.860
What's this about?

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:13.470
I haven't seen Kondo-san in a week.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:15.320
Do you know anything?

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:17.670
W-We don't know anything, right?

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:18.770
We know nothing at all.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:20.750
No clue at all.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:22.760
L-Let's move on.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:23.660
Ah!

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:24.780
This is from Zenzo-san.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.470
I need to talk with Sarutobi about a job,

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:29.540
but I haven't been able to reach her for a week.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:31.780
Have you seen her around?

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:39.780
The people who sent out fake wedding notices are disappearing one after another...

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.160
It's not related.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.420
I mean, look at this.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:48.810
<b>Hatsu Hasegawa</b>

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.580
I can't reach my husband.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:47.120
I found some of my husband's belongings by the river.

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:48.810
Do you know anything?

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:49.720
Yeah?

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:52.290
Hasegawa-san's missing and he wasn't involved in that crap.

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:53.120
It's okay.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:54.500
It's not okay!

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:57.680
He's missing for a completely different reason!

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:59.820
I have a really bad feeling about this.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:01.140
Hasegawa-san aside,

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:02.200
the other two must have gotten into some kind New-Year-card-related trouble.

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:03.710
It's not related.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.700
Oh, there's one from the boss lady.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:09.840
I am unable to wish you a happy new year in this time of mourning.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:13.270
In December, our pet gorilla and bitch passed away.

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:14.320
This year will be...

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:16.510
You had pets?

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:17.590
We did.

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:19.330
I've never seen them before.

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:22.180
There was that "I'm first, Otae" message.

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:24.020
That must have pissed her off.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:26.630
P-Please don't tell anyone.

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:28.720
Well, it's not exactly a secret.

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:31.450
I haven't seen Kondo-san in a week.

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:35.010
Do you know anything about someone's older sister killing him?

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:37.670
How many older sisters are there in this show?!

00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:39.290
And look, there's one from Yamazaki.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:39.920
What?!

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:41.420
Yamazaki-san?!

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:44.860
<b>Anpan! Anpan! Anpan!</b>

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:44.860
What the hell happened to Yamazaki-san?!

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:47.870
Gin-chan, there's a really weird New Year's card.

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:49.660
From Gondo.

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:51.660
Where the hell is Gondo?

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:53.570
Do we know anyone there?

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:55.460
It's from someone called Mamyudapao.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:57.450
I'm 100% positive that we don't know this person!

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:59.400
I'm 100% positive that this is a complete stranger!

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:00.650
Let me read it.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:03.760
My name is Mamudapao Hasegawa.

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:05.660
It's just Hasegawa-san!

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:07.760
How far did the river carry him?!

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.950
When I came to this place,

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:14.770
I could only remember the words Hasegawa and oldsocks.

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:16.920
You've got it wrong!

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:18.690
It's orthodox!

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:24.280
Mamudapao was the name given to me by the Hingromaxon chief who found me.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:26.180
It means floating log,

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:27.310
drifter,

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:28.190
freeter,

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:29.360
Nintendo,

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.800
and sinking old man.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.090
There are too many meanings!

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:34.540
The last one contradicts the first one!

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:36.680
Mamudapao.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:38.510
Everyone calls me Madao for short.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:41.050
So they still call you Madao in the end!

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:45.050
The people of the Hingromaxon tribe are very kind.

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:49.170
They were willing to share their fruit with a complete stranger.

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:51.060
They clearly hate you!

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:55.460
I had no memories, but I was...

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:56.800
...satisfied with my life here.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:58.900
This man is the definition of a masochist!

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:03.160
I had a mission before I lost my memories.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:04.920
But I can't remember what it was.

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:10.260
When I washed ashore, I was holding a piece of paper with some strange characters.

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:12.930
Will they help unlock my memories?

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:15.650
I showed the piece of paper to the chief,

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:17.920
and he said that he'd seen something similar before.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:23.800
The Hingromaxon were engaged in a turf war with two other tribes.

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:28.050
He'd seen the other chiefs with similar pieces of paper.

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:34.430
They are also Madao, Mamudapao who
came ashore from a different world like you.

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:38.300
They used their fearsome strength to rise to power

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:41.620
and began to invade our sacred forest.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:43.590
They are monsters.

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:46.250
Our tribe stands no chance against them.

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:47.900
But Madao,

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:50.990
since you also came from a different world...

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:53.490
I may die.

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:58.560
But if I choose to live without fulfilling my duty,

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:01.760
I might as well be dead!

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:03.470
Move it!

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:04.670
Outta the way!

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:07.130
Don't interfere with our crusade!

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:09.550
Stop this pointless war.

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:11.880
We are all children of this planet.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:13.190
One big family.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.670
Don't lump me in with you wretches!

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:19.130
Our tribe is meant to rule the sacred forest!

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:20.350
No.

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:23.670
I'm sure that we share the same purpose.

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:25.160
That's...

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:27.150
I've always wondered who I was...

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:29.930
Wondered what I was meant to do...

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:31.740
For a very long time...

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:35.060
Ever since I was wrapped up in a mat and washed away...

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:38.300
I always thought I was alone...

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:42.330
The next thing I knew, the three of us were holding each other in tears.

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:47.410
And without a word, we each took out our pieces of paper.

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:51.150
They were completely different and couldn't be pieced together,

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:54.850
but our fragmented memories were united.

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:56.760
Chief, what about the crusade?

00:11:56.780 --> 00:11:59.450
I don't have time for that nonsense.

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:01.460
What are you going to do then?

00:12:01.460 --> 00:12:03.040
That should be obvious.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:07.440
Let's write a New Year's card together.

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:09.870
Happy New Year!

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:12.210
We have new members in the family!

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:18.310
Gin-san, there's also this...

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:23.610
I was on standby on a raft to Gondo,

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:24.710
<b>Kotaro Katsura</b>

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:25.410
but I ended up in Rhone.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:30.210
Gin-chan, how should we respond?

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:35.010
<b>The Gintama anime wasn't able to ride the Ryomaden wave.</b>

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:33.190
Make copies of this to send to everyone.

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:40.980
"I only received one chocolate this year. From my mom..."

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:45.270
"I win. I got two. Including my sister..."

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:49.230
If anyone out there starts gloating the day after Valentine's,

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:51.440
starting next year, execute 'em.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:57.270
That joke is as old as chocolate and moms.

00:12:57.270 --> 00:12:58.320
Cut the crap.

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:01.450
Don't put on airs by joking around to show that you don't care!

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:02.750
I'm sick of it!

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:08.160
The practice of passing chocolate around like idiots!

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:09.550
Enough of this farce!

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:11.670
Starting next year,

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:13.680
execute every single person who gives or receives chocolate!

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.220
Is that your final answer?

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:17.650
That's my final answer!

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:21.860
Final answer, my ass!

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.430
Somebody bring me some chocolate!

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:24.820
This makes no sense at all!

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:27.240
Everything was the same as the first half!

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.620
There was a stack of New Year's cards after the scene change!

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:31.610
So why isn't there any chocolate here?!

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:32.850
I want chocolate!

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:34.690
No need for love!

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:37.570
Just give me sugar!

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:40.540
I want love and that's my final answer!

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.920
Wait, can I ask the audience?

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:45.580
You can spend the rest of your life on the phone with Regis.

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:51.010
Sorry about making you come with me.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:54.780
I've heard that Valentine's is when girls give chocolate to the people they like.

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:57.300
Does that mean you like a whole bunch of people?

00:13:57.300 --> 00:14:00.420
These are just for passing out to our customers.

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:01.930
As for the people I like...

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:03.310
Here.

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:04.800
Boss lady!

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:07.040
I love you lots!

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:09.080
But I don't have any chocolate for you.

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:10.440
It's okay.

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:13.320
You should find a nice man to give your chocolate to.

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:15.530
But there's nobody.

00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:18.240
You could give chocolate to Gin-san and Shin-chan this time.

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:19.660
What? Forget it.

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:22.190
I don't really like those morons.

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:25.650
They'll probably gripe about not wanting any chocolate from a little brat.

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:27.290
That's not true.

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:32.340
I'm sure they'll be surprised, even thrilled, if you give them chocolate.

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:36.440
They don't need me when people like Sa-chan will give them some.

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:37.720
Thanks for the chocolate.

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:39.420
Ah, Kagura-chan.

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:59.360
Hey, why are you so fidgety, Kagura?

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:01.100
I-I'm not!

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:02.960
Don't tell me that...

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:08.170
...you need to poop?

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:09.270
Move it then.

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:10.790
Constipation is bad for beauty.

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:15.130
<b>Odd Jobs Gin-chan</b>

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:19.060
Ka-Kagura-chan!

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:21.120
Is this what I think it is?!

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:21.820
Chocolate.

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:23.400
R-Really?!

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:24.130
Mom!

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:26.250
She gave me chocolate!

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:29.810
Thank you for being so thoughtful.

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:31.080
It's nothing.

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:33.330
This doesn't have boogers or anything inside, right?

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:34.500
It's safe to eat?

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:36.610
It's obviously safe. Want me to kill you?

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:40.060
You're much more chic than I thought.

00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:42.080
You have the potential to become a courtesan.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:43.430
Really?

00:15:43.430 --> 00:15:47.160
Then I should quit working at that dump and move here.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:49.820
Hey, can I eat this?

00:15:49.820 --> 00:15:51.490
I see sesame seeds for some reason.

00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:53.580
Don't touch those.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:56.190
Boogers can make you sick.

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:57.490
Enough already!

00:15:57.490 --> 00:16:00.300
Do you people think I'm some kind of monster?!

00:16:00.550 --> 00:16:02.720
Hinowa, I'm heading out for a bit.

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:04.300
Hey, wait!

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:05.990
Give that back!

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:07.490
Excuse me.

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:09.680
I'd like to buy that big chocolate heart.

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:10.600
Sure thing.

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:13.110
Hey, what are you doing, Tsu-ki?

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:17.690
Hinowa actually told me to give you guys chocolate from Yoshiwara.

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:21.240
Can you take care of that for me?

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:25.240
It'll be easier for you to hand yours over with mine.

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:26.650
Tsu-ki!

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:28.530
You're so sharp!

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:30.750
Completely different from that clueless numbskull with wavy hair!

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:34.190
But, I'd really appreciate it if you would come with me.

00:16:34.190 --> 00:16:35.680
I-I can't help you there.

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:37.960
Why? You also think it's embarrassing?

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:40.700
Wh-Why would I be embarrassed?!

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:43.710
I don't give a damn about Valentine's.

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:47.260
I only bought this chocolate because I was ordered to, not because I wanted to...

00:16:46.010 --> 00:16:47.260
<b>You look embarrassed.</b>

00:16:47.260 --> 00:16:48.990
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:50.710
Well, I understand.

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:52.790
I'll let them know how you feel.

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:55.270
<b>From Tsu-ki with love</b>

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:55.270
<b>To Odd Jobs</b>

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:55.270
What do you think you're doing?!

00:16:55.270 --> 00:16:58.420
Well, she kept calling you Tsu-ki,

00:16:58.420 --> 00:17:00.110
so I decided to add a little something special.

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:00.110
<b>You're not helping!</b>

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:02.060
Say that it's from everyone in Yoshiwara!

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:02.970
I apologize.

00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:03.970
I'll get that fixed real quick,

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:05.450
so please wait, Tsu-ki.

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:07.690
Why are you calling me Tsu-ki?!

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:10.300
Hey, I'm starting to get worried,

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:12.070
so mind if I tag along?

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:13.200
Yay!

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:17.020
Um, would you like to try some while you're waiting?

00:17:17.020 --> 00:17:21.700
Man, everybody loves to make assumptions.

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:23.090
That looks good.

00:17:23.090 --> 00:17:24.900
Can I try one?

00:17:24.900 --> 00:17:26.280
Sorry.

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:27.790
These are whiskey bonbons,

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:30.170
and you're still too young.

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:35.710
We're not interested in a newspaper subscription.

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:38.650
Excuse me, is Gintoki-kun here?

00:17:38.650 --> 00:17:40.650
Gosh, I went and opened my mouth!

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:41.840
Oh, dear.

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:43.490
My heart is pounding...

00:17:43.490 --> 00:17:44.790
This is too much for me.

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:46.160
It's too embarrassing...

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:50.420
In your dreams, sucker!

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:56.040
You want us to hand over our chocolate together?

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:59.250
Yeah, I've tried a couple times and failed.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:00.820
Don't be a fool?

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:02.060
Why would we confess our feelings as a group?

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:03.460
Are we still in middle school?

00:18:03.460 --> 00:18:05.180
We're just going to give them chocolate.

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:08.170
But I'm having trouble because it's so embarrassing.

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:11.560
I need help from an insensitive woman like you.

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:14.870
I've never been so insulted while being asked for a favor.

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:16.090
Besides!

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:18.550
Tsu-ki, how could you let this happen?

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:19.570
Is that the power of 10th place?

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:21.220
Is that what it takes to place 10th?

00:18:21.220 --> 00:18:23.280
You're still upset about that?

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:25.830
I would never choose to help a rival,

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:29.630
but you girls are so pathetic that there's no threat at all.

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:34.790
First, strip naked and coat yourself in this chocolate.

00:18:34.790 --> 00:18:36.650
That's where it all begins.

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:37.890
That's where it all begins?

00:18:37.890 --> 00:18:39.180
More like that's where it all ends.

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:40.970
Lose the innocent girl act!

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:43.040
Don't you realize that I'm telling you to stop feeling ashamed?!

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:43.880
I'm willing to stop feeling ashamed,

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:46.090
but I won't stop behaving like a proper human being.

00:18:46.090 --> 00:18:47.170
What?!

00:18:47.170 --> 00:18:49.260
Don't you know that Cleopatra got naked

00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:53.560
and lotioned herself up inside a rolled-up rug for the sake of seducing the king?!

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:55.300
We aren't trying to seduce anyone!

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:58.330
We just want to give them chocolate!

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:00.610
Fine.

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:02.560
We'll do this the normal way.

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:05.420
Honestly, you're so dull.

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:07.320
Then I'll press the doorbell...

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:10.910
Um...

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:12.950
Why are you lined up behind me?

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:14.850
How shy are you?!

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:16.180
Can you stop that?!

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:18.050
You're making me nervous!

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:19.280
I'm going to press the doorbell now.

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:19.920
Are you ready?

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:27.160
Sa-chan!

00:19:27.170 --> 00:19:28.970
Hey! What was that?!

00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:30.120
Actually...

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:31.840
Now that I think about it...

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:34.840
I've never tried doing it the normal way,

00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:36.890
so I don't know what to say.

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:39.440
Didn't you just lecture me about Cleopatra?!

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:40.730
Sorry! I can't do it!

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:41.250
You go, Tsu-ki!

00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:42.260
I feel so embarrassed!

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:43.480
It's too late for that now!

00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:45.080
Kagura, you go.

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:45.740
Isn't this your home?

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:46.610
Hey!

00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:49.450
Why do you think I brought you with me?!

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:52.490
Where did Kagura-chan go?

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:57.010
She ran off somewhere to take a dump.

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:58.170
Huh?

00:19:58.170 --> 00:19:59.800
Wasn't there someone here?

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:02.560
No, nobody's here.

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:06.950
Was this can here earlier?

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:08.170
Whatever.

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:23.480
Um, I'd appreciate it if you left this in front of Odd Jobs when you get a chance.

00:20:23.710 --> 00:20:26.430
Sorry that I wasn't any help.

00:20:26.860 --> 00:20:29.650
I appreciate it!

00:20:35.490 --> 00:20:37.990
<b>To Gin-chan and Shinpachi --Kagura</b>

00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:44.880
I'm sorry.

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:48.670
I suppose I shouldn't have said anything.

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:50.700
Nah.

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:54.180
It was fun to do girly stuff with them.

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:57.000
Though it's not very me.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:58.430
It's better this way.

00:20:58.430 --> 00:21:00.140
Kagura-chan...

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:03.720
You could have asked me to come along.

00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:05.100
I have some extra chocolate for them.

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:08.350
But if you aren't going to give them yours, I won't either.

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:09.310
It's okay.

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:11.730
I'll give them yours with the other ones.

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:14.100
But what about you?

00:21:14.770 --> 00:21:16.480
It's okay.

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:20.650
I don't need to use chocolate

00:21:20.650 --> 00:21:25.580
to show off my planet-sized love!

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:29.270
Right?

00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:32.090
That's right.

00:21:33.130 --> 00:21:35.340
Counting the ones that don't count, I got three...

00:21:38.430 --> 00:21:41.430
We didn't get a single one this year.

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:43.140
That's my final answer.

00:21:45.870 --> 00:21:48.390
There were three outside the door.

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:49.820
Isn't that nice?

00:21:50.070 --> 00:21:51.030
Huh?! What?!

00:21:51.020 --> 00:21:51.440
No way!

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:52.130
From who?!

00:21:52.130 --> 00:21:53.070
For who?!

00:21:52.780 --> 00:21:56.490
<b>Sugar Content</b>

00:21:53.070 --> 00:21:54.590
Get your grubby paws off them!

00:21:54.590 --> 00:21:56.490
They're obviously for me!

00:21:58.240 --> 00:22:01.700
<b>For Gin-san and Four-Eyes</b>

00:21:58.240 --> 00:22:01.700
<b>From Kagura</b>

00:21:58.240 --> 00:22:01.700
<b>From Kagura with love</b>

00:21:58.240 --> 00:22:01.700
<b>To Gintoki and Shinpachi</b>

00:21:58.240 --> 00:22:01.700
<b>I love Gin-chan and Shinpachi
Kagura</b>

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:03.510
Shinpachi...

00:22:04.290 --> 00:22:06.290
We got four this year.

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:09.030
That's my final answer.

00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:12.920
The Heart Comes Before Chocolate

00:23:40.010 --> 00:23:44.970
Next Episode

00:23:40.010 --> 00:23:44.970
Meals Should Be Balanced

00:23:40.580 --> 00:23:41.700
Sorry about the confusion.

00:23:41.700 --> 00:23:45.370
After next week, you'll finally understand all the fuss about anpan.
